{"seq":3,"slug":"toolsmith-mindset","title":"工具匠人哲学","stage":"DONE","category":"personal-systems","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset","rating":{"composite":4.14,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.2,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.7,"verdict":"consider","uScore":4.25}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"工具匠人哲学-简介\">工具匠人哲学 简介</h1><p>工具匠人哲学探讨程序员为何应该自制工具、如何从简单脚本逐步演进为成熟产品，以及如何将个人工具开源回馈社区。历史上无数改变世界的开发者工具——curl、grep、jq、ripgrep——最初都诞生于某位程序员解决自身痛点的冲动。这种&quot;自己的问题自己解决&quot;的匠人精神，不仅提升了个人生产力，更塑造了整个软件行业的基础设施。</p>\n<p>本知识库面向所有希望从&quot;工具消费者&quot;转变为&quot;工具创造者&quot;的开发者。无论你是刚开始写 shell 脚本的初学者，还是已经维护多个 CLI 工具的资深开发者，都能在这里找到系统性的方法论和实践指导。</p>\n<p><strong>第一章 工具匠人理念</strong> 从哲学层面剖析为什么程序员应该自制工具，探讨工具思维与消费思维的根本差异，并建立&quot;复合收益&quot;的心智模型——你今天花一小时写的脚本，未来可能为你节省数千小时。</p>\n<p><strong>第二章 渐进式工具开发</strong> 提供从脚本到 CLI、从 CLI 到 TUI/GUI、从个人工具到开源产品的完整演进路径。每一步都有清晰的判断标准和实操指南，帮助你在合适的时机做出合适的升级决策。</p>\n<p><strong>第三章 工具设计原则</strong> 深入讲解 Unix 哲学在现代工具开发中的应用、可组合性设计的核心模式，以及如何从人机工程学角度打造真正好用的开发者工具。</p>\n<p><strong>第四章 开源你的工具</strong> 覆盖从&quot;个人脚本&quot;到&quot;开源项目&quot;的完整转型路径，包括开源准备清单、社区建设策略、长期维护与版本演进的最佳实践。</p>\n<p>推荐学习路径：先从第一章建立理念基础，然后按顺序学习后续章节。如果你已经有工具开发经验，可以直接跳到第三章或第四章获取进阶指导。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"toolsmith-philosophy","title":"工具匠人理念","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/toolsmith-philosophy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-build-your-own-tools","title":"为什么自制工具","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/toolsmith-philosophy/why-build-your-own-tools"},{"seq":2,"slug":"tool-thinking-vs-consumer-thinking","title":"工具思维 vs 消费思维","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/toolsmith-philosophy/tool-thinking-vs-consumer-thinking"},{"seq":3,"slug":"compound-returns-model","title":"复合收益模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/toolsmith-philosophy/compound-returns-model"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"progressive-tooling","title":"渐进式工具开发","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/progressive-tooling","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"from-script-to-cli","title":"从脚本到 CLI","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/progressive-tooling/from-script-to-cli"},{"seq":2,"slug":"from-cli-to-tui-gui","title":"从 CLI 到 TUI/GUI","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/progressive-tooling/from-cli-to-tui-gui"},{"seq":3,"slug":"from-personal-to-open-source","title":"从个人工具到开源产品","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/progressive-tooling/from-personal-to-open-source"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"tool-design-principles","title":"工具设计原则","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/tool-design-principles","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"unix-philosophy-applied","title":"Unix 哲学应用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/tool-design-principles/unix-philosophy-applied"},{"seq":2,"slug":"composability-design","title":"可组合性设计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/tool-design-principles/composability-design"},{"seq":3,"slug":"developer-ergonomics","title":"人机工程学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/tool-design-principles/developer-ergonomics"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"open-source-your-tools","title":"开源你的工具","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/open-source-your-tools","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"open-source-readiness-checklist","title":"开源准备清单","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/open-source-your-tools/open-source-readiness-checklist"},{"seq":2,"slug":"community-building","title":"社区建设","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/open-source-your-tools/community-building"},{"seq":3,"slug":"maintenance-evolution-strategy","title":"维护与演进策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/personal-systems/toolsmith-mindset/open-source-your-tools/maintenance-evolution-strategy"}]}]}